  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "宋明心性之學",
    "sub_ename": "SONG-MING LEARNING OF THE MIND AND NATURE",
    "describe_ch": "本課程聚焦於宋明理學的核心——「心性之學」。自20世紀港臺新儒家提出宋明儒學為繼先秦孔孟之後的思想高峰以來，朱熹（1130-1200）與王守仁（1472-1529）便被視為兩大典型代表。朱熹強調格物致知、理在事先；王守仁則主張心即理、知行合一。本課程以二人思想為主軸，選讀其代表性文獻，並探討相關主題，從而理解心性之學的理論內涵與歷史意義。藉此，學生能深化對儒學、理學及中國思想史發展的掌握，並思考心性論在今日的啟發。",
    "describe_eh": "This course centers on the core of Song-Ming Neo-Confucianism: the \"Learning of the Mind and Nature.\" Since the twentieth-century New Confucians in Hong Kong and Taiwan proposed that Song-Ming Confucianism represents the second peak of Chinese thought after the pre-Qin era of Confucius and Mencius, Zhu Xi (1130–1200) and Wang Shouren (1472–1529) have been regarded as two paradigmatic figures. Zhu Xi emphasized the investigation of things and the extension of knowledge, holding that principle (li) precedes and transcends phenomena; Wang Shouren, by contrast, advocated the identity of mind and principle, as well as the unity of knowledge and action. Taking their thought as the main axis, this course selects and reads representative texts from both thinkers and explores related themes, thereby illuminating the theoretical content and historical significance of the Learning of Mind and Nature. Through this approach, students will deepen their understanding of Confucianism, Neo-Confucianism, and the development of Chinese intellectual history, while also reflecting on the relevance of theories of mind and nature for contemporary thought.",
    "pre_subname": "",
    "pre_sub_id3": null,
    "pre_sub_ename": "",
    "pre_describe": null,
    "pre_describe_en": null,
    "scr_credit": 2.0
  },
  "targets": [
    {
      "seq": 1,
      "describe_ch": "透過閱讀朱熹與王守仁的主要文獻，理解其對「理」與「心」的不同詮釋，並能比較兩大思想體系的異同",
      "describe_en": "Through close reading of the major works of Zhu Xi and Wang Yangming, this course aims to elucidate their distinct interpretations of li and xin, and to compare the similarities and differences between these two major intellectual systems"
    },
    {
      "seq": 2,
      "describe_ch": "建立學生對宋明理學在中國思想史中地位與意義的宏觀視野，理解其與先秦儒學之承續與差異",
      "describe_en": "To cultivate students' macro-perspective on the position and significance of Song-Ming Neo-Confucianism in the history of Chinese thought, and to understand its continuities and departures from pre-Qin Confucianism."
    },
    {
      "seq": 3,
      "describe_ch": "引導學生思考「心性之學」對當代社會與個人修養的啟發，並能提出具有現實關懷的理論反思與應用",
      "describe_en": "To guide students to critically reflect on how the Learning of the Mind and Nature can inform contemporary society and self-cultivation, and to develop theoretically informed reflections with practical implications."
    }
  ],
